<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila Central Bank eases loan rules for housing.</title>
<headline>Manila Central Bank eases loan rules for housing.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine Central Bank said on Thursday the Monetary Board had relaxed its rules on bank loans for low and medium-cost homes.</p>
<p>Central Bank governor Gabriel Singson said in a circular that loans of up to 3.5 million pesos to finance the purchase or improvement of residential units would now be excluded from the recently imposed 20 percent limit on the total a bank could lend to the property sector.</p>
</text>
